 "text": "Hey, how are you feeling? That's lovely. Many charity warehouses need tools more than something you' end up using once. Would they accept a donation box? Buy them a box of their favourite cookie, and in it a small box of sweets from the shop that's closing down. The family will have the cookie, and the shop will get a proper send off. Keep it in the kitchen where everyone passes, and put a note in each box asking people to ask ahead if doubtful. It teaches little ones about sharing and being kind, and you're doing it together as a family.",
